1. Research question

Does the amount of amino acid intake after cardiac surgery affect the development of acute kidney injury (AKI)?
Primary outcome: new AKI diagnosed within the first 4 days after ICU admission.
Secondary outcome: new AKI diagnosed on days 5–6 after ICU admission.

2. Data

Dataset: 350 patients, high data quality.
Patients with AKI before surgery are excluded.
Statistical challenge: 
10–15% of patients die after surgery. For these patients, 
it cannot be observed whether protein intake would have affected kidney function (risk of selection bias).
Randomized trials are the preferred design for this question.

